# Upstream source is not vendored. This port re-expresses the assertions of the
# upstream samples against cleat's Go SDK. See ../../docs/licensing.md.
#
# THE LICENCE FIELD WAS WRONG IN THIS REPO BEFORE THIS PORT EXISTED.
# ports/README.md listed this upstream as MIT. It is Apache-2.0.
#
# Worth recording how the error survived, because the check that would catch it
# is the one people trust:
#
#     gh api repos/temporalio/samples-go --jq .license.spdx_id
#     NOASSERTION
#
# GitHub cannot classify the file, because LICENSE is a short-form Apache
# NOTICE -- "Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0" plus the URL --
# rather than the full licence text its classifier matches against. So the
# programmatic answer is "Other", the table said MIT, and the file says
# Apache-2.0. Three answers; only reading the file settles it.
#
# Both wrong answers are dangerous in different directions: NOASSERTION reads
# as "no licence" and would have excluded a permissively licensed upstream,
# and MIT reads as permissive-and-checked when nobody had checked.
